          "text": "Perianal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right lateral anal margin has an approximately 1.5–2 cm tense, bluish, exquisitely tender swelling, consistent with thrombosed external haemorrhoid/perianal haematoma. Overlying skin intact, with no ulceration, necrosis, or discharge. No surrounding erythema or induration and no features of perianal abscess or cellulitis. No other fissures, warts, or lesions."
